Tasks: dalogin SQLAccess CDI datasource injection

Phase 1 — Preconditions (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Confirm `dalogin-datasource-legacy-removal` is complete (single pooled connection path).
- [ ] Inventory all 21 data-access methods and their `ServletContext` usage.
- [ ] Classify each `ServletContext` parameter as datasource-only or genuinely needed.
- [ ] Confirm `dalogin-datasource-legacy-removal` narrowed `getConnection()` to `throws SQLException`.
- [ ] Record which methods declare `throws Exception` and which of those handle their own `SQLException`.
- [ ] Inventory all 16 caller files and group them by caller type.
- [ ] Record baseline counts: 21 connection and all statement try-with-resources blocks, 11 bare result sets.
- [ ] Capture the current SQL text so the post-pass diff can be proven empty.

Phase 2 — Field injection confirmation (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebServlet` classes under `quarkus-undertow`.
- [ ] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebFilter` classes (`ChangePswFilter`, `ActiveVoucherFilter`).
- [ ] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebListener` classes (`CustomHttpSessionListener`).
- [ ] Confirm no caller in this module needs the programmatic CDI lookup escape hatch.

Execution rule (applies to Phases 3–6)
- All production code changes land in ONE pass. Do not compile, run, or smoke-test partway through.
- Do not add a delegation shim, compatibility overload, or temporary static forwarder.
- The module is expected to be uncompilable until Phase 6. That is accepted and intended.

Phase 3 — Bean foundation (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Create the final `@ApplicationScoped` family beans with injected `DataSource`.
- [ ] Implement connection acquisition directly in the final owning families.
- [ ] Add the documented lookup helper for non-CDI-capable callers.
- [ ] Confirm no delegation shim or temporary static forwarder was introduced.

Phase 4 — Method migration (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Move user/account methods directly to the final login/registration bean.
- [ ] Move voucher methods directly to the final voucher bean.
- [ ] Move device/session/token methods directly to the merged final bean.
- [ ] Move password-reset methods directly to the final password-reset bean.
- [ ] Drop datasource-only `ServletContext` parameters.
- [ ] Keep `generateUUID`, `logSQLException`, `ignoreSQLException`, and `jsonSQLError` static and connection-free.
- [ ] Confirm every migrated method still uses try-with-resources.
- [ ] Confirm no SQL text, parameter order, or result mapping changed.

Phase 4b — Connection-close hardening (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Confirm the bean holds no `Connection` field and caches no connection.
- [ ] Confirm all 21 connection acquisitions remain in try-with-resources.
- [ ] Confirm all statement try-with-resources blocks were preserved, including nested `cstmt2` cases.
- [ ] Convert all 11 bare `ResultSet` locals to try-with-resources.
- [ ] Convert nested result sets (`rs2` in `getForgotPswToken`) to try-with-resources.
- [ ] Add explicit `rollback()` to the `wrapUpRegistration` failure path.
- [ ] Add `SqlSupport.rollbackQuietly` and `restoreAutoCommit` so cleanup cannot propagate.
- [ ] Confirm a failing `rollback()` cannot replace the method's return value or hide the original exception.
- [ ] Narrow each migrated method from `throws Exception` to the reachable exception, or to none.
- [ ] Confirm no caller was forced to handle more than before.
- [ ] Confirm no catch block swallows without logging through `SqlSupport.logSQLException`.
- [ ] Confirm `autoCommit` cannot leak as `false` to the next pool borrower.
- [ ] Confirm no `@PreDestroy` or shutdown hook closes connections.
- [ ] Confirm no `closeConnection()` equivalent was reintroduced into the bean.
- [ ] Confirm no `finally` block was added to work around missing try-with-resources.

Phase 5 — Caller migration and legacy deletion (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Migrate authentication and session callers to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Migrate registration and voucher callers to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Migrate password-change and reset callers to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Migrate purchase-related callers to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Migrate `CustomHttpSessionListener` to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Migrate both filters to `@Inject` field injection.
- [ ] Convert every `SQLAccess.<method>(..., context)` call site to an injected-field instance call.
- [ ] Confirm zero remaining callers use a programmatic CDI lookup.
- [ ] Remove the `"DBManager"` servlet-context attribute publication.
- [ ] Remove `DBConnectionManager` if it has no remaining references.
- [ ] Confirm no production code reads `"DBManager"` from the servlet context.

