- [ ] Confirm it passes without `mbook` or `mbooks` running.
- [ ] Confirm the test hits `dalogin-quarkus` directly, not the Apache reverse proxy.
- [ ] Skip `loginThenRetrieveUser`; it calls downstream mbook, which is not required here.

Phase 7 — Static verification (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Diff SQL text before and after; confirm the diff is empty.
- [ ] Re-count try-with-resources blocks: connections 21 and statements match baseline.
- [ ] Confirm result-set try-with-resources rose from 0 to 11.
- [ ] Confirm zero bare `ResultSet` locals remain.
- [ ] Confirm by inspection that `wrapUpRegistration` rolls back on its failure path.
- [ ] Confirm by inspection that `autoCommit` cannot leak `false` to the next pool borrower.
- [ ] Confirm zero `throws Exception` declarations remain on migrated data-access methods.
- [ ] Confirm `wrapUpRegistration` still rolls back; the business behavior must survive the refactor.
- [ ] Confirm result-set scope narrowing did not change any returned value.

Phase 8 — Closure (`@security-specialist` + `@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Confirm the change was delivered as a single pass with no shim in any reviewable state.
- [ ] Confirm no new shared mutable static state was introduced.
- [ ] Confirm connection handling introduces no credential logging.
